# `makefiles/terraform.mk` keeps REPORT_PATH at its default `build/reports/`, which
# `common` already covers. This is what its `test` target writes besides the JUnit report.

# `terraform.mk:test` runs `terraform init -backend=false` in the module under test, which
# vendors provider binaries and module sources into `.terraform/`. Unanchored so it matches
# at any depth, which is also what every published Terraform `.gitignore` does.
#
# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT here: it pins provider versions and is meant
# to be committed.
#
# `/build/.terraform-plugin-cache/` is deliberately not here either -- only the validate
# tier writes it, and `terra.mk` is the sole `.mk` that exposes that tier
# (`test-validate`). Fragments follow evidence, not symmetry.
.terraform/
